(1428633, 184184, 31230, '<td valign="top">Like that you can see her expression and see that she is making a decision.  Very nice work</td>', 'Like that you can see her expression and see that she is making a decision.  Very nice work', '2005-06-02 07:36:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(1428634, 183998, 31230, '<td valign="top">Nice expressive photo.  I can clearly see by her face that she is making a decision.  The two different shoes help too, but love her face.</td>', 'Nice expressive photo.  I can clearly see by her face that she is making a decision.  The two different shoes help too, but love her face.', '2005-06-02 07:39:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(1428636, 182580, 31230, '<td valign="top">Very nice, before I even scrolled down to see the his bowl, I could tell from his facial expression that he was deciding something. Then I read your title.  Very nice work.</td>', 'Very nice, before I even scrolled down to see the his bowl, I could tell from his facial expression that he was deciding something. Then I read your title.  Very nice work.', '2005-06-02 07:41:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(1428645, 183100, 11738, '<td valign="top">Colours seem a bit washed out on this one.  Playing with curves or contrast could have helped this image to pop a bit more.  Vertical lines in background are also a bit distracting.</td>', 'Colours seem a bit washed out on this one.  Playing with curves or contrast could have helped this image to pop a bit more.  Vertical lines in background are also a bit distracting.', '2005-06-02 07:54:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(1428658, 183475, 37851, '<td valign="top">I dont see this picture as being a decision.</td>', 'I dont see this picture as being a decision.', '2005-06-02 08:15:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1428659, 183950, 37851, '<td valign="top">I dont understand how this is a decision.</td>', 'I dont understand how this is a decision.', '2005-06-02 08:17:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(1428663, 182659, 34192, '<td valign="top">interesting take on the challenge.  I would have preferred the image to be completely in focus rather than just the points, but that is my opinion - you may have been going for something different.  The lighting is a little harsh and in some spots blows out the detail slightly.  Good luck in the challenge!</td>', 'interesting take on the challenge.  I would have preferred the image to be completely in focus rather than just the points, but that is my opinion - you may have been going for something different.  The lighting is a little harsh and in some spots blows out the detail slightly.  Good luck in the challenge!', '2005-06-02 08:20:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(1428669, 184198, 34192, '<td valign="top">wow - mine haven''t even budded yet!  Not sure what would improve this image for me - there are many ways to go with this.  I don''t know if your camera is capable, but a really short DOF would have blurred the background so the flower stands out more.  You may also try getting in closer - but that would only work if you have macro mode.  The red looks to be a little oversaturated but it does make the flower stand out!  Good luck in the challenge!</td>', 'wow - mine haven''t even budded yet!  Not sure what would improve this image for me - there are many ways to go with this.  I don''t know if your camera is capable, but a really short DOF would have blurred the background so the flower stands out more.  You may also try getting in closer - but that would only work if you have macro mode.  The red looks to be a little oversaturated but it does make the flower stand out!  Good luck in the challenge!', '2005-06-02 08:24:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(1428682, 183623, 35044, '<td valign="top">I am making this comment on a number of votes, but please don''t hold that against me: I just wanted to let you know why I gave you a relatively low score in this challenge.  I have approached voting with the starting point that the photograph should stand on its own (ie without the title), and have as a focal point a decision (ie I should look at this photo and one of the main things that I should be thinking about when looking at the photo is, "there is a decision just made, being made, or about to be made, and this photo captures that moment".  Ideally, I''d love to be provoked by the image into thinking that "the essence of this photo is the decision it portrays".<br/> <br/>Unfortunately, absent the title, I would not have guessed that your photo was intended to capture a "decision".  As the rules state, I am voting with high regard to the challenge description.  However, I am explaining why in case you were left wondering why your score is not doing was well as you expected!<br/> <br/>Specific to your picture, I would add that<br/>the highlights in the controller are overexposed and the image might have been more interesting if we coud have seen the model''s face (eg game reflecting in his eyes...)<br/> <br/></td>', 'I am making this comment on a number of votes, but please don''t hold that against me: I just wanted to let you know why I gave you a relatively low score in this challenge.  I have approached voting with the starting point that the photograph should stand on its own (ie without the title), and have as a focal point a decision (ie I should look at this photo and one of the main things that I should be thinking about when looking at the photo is, "there is a decision just made, being made, or about to be made, and this photo captures that moment".  Ideally, I''d love to be provoked by the image into thinking that "the essence of this photo is the decision it portrays". Unfortunately, absent the title, 