(1431092, 182880, 38401, '<td valign="top">I don''t feel that the image conveys instantly recognizable decision. Great pic. I think the problem is the title does most of the work, now if the title and the photo went hand in hand... this would have done much better.</td>', 'I don''t feel that the image conveys instantly recognizable decision. Great pic. I think the problem is the title does most of the work, now if the title and the photo went hand in hand... this would have done much better.', '2005-06-03 10:45:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(1431098, 184147, 38401, '<td valign="top">I don''t feel that the image conveys instantly recognizable decision. I also am not sure I fully understand the meaning of the title... my understanding of the photo is hurt by this. I also do not feel motivated to make any decisions, nor do I see a subject making decisions.</td>', 'I don''t feel that the image conveys instantly recognizable decision. I also am not sure I fully understand the meaning of the title... my understanding of the photo is hurt by this. I also do not feel motivated to make any decisions, nor do I see a subject making decisions.', '2005-06-03 10:47:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(1431105, 183563, 38401, '<td valign="top">I went back and rethought this, personally I would have preferred to see someones hand in the photo to boot, but I have to say that the title does give me the impression that ''someone'' is behind the decision to cut the red wire. So I am moving this up to a 5. This is the best of the wire cutting photos so far.</td>', 'I went back and rethought this, personally I would have preferred to see someones hand in the photo to boot, but I have to say that the title does give me the impression that ''someone'' is behind the decision to cut the red wire. So I am moving this up to a 5. This is the best of the wire cutting photos so far.', '2005-06-03 10:50:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(1431123, 183756, 38401, '<td valign="top">I don''t feel that the image conveys instantly recognizable decision. The wedding ring does tell us that a decision has been made, but It''s not easy to say that that is true. Rather a better photo in ''my opinion'' would have been the bride and groom slipping the rings on their hands... a close up of the hands slipping the rings on, because it denotes the ''action'' of deciding to commit forever. Because making a decision is an action, I think the photos should denote action.</td>', 'I don''t feel that the image conveys instantly recognizable decision. The wedding ring does tell us that a decision has been made, but It''s not easy to say that that is true. Rather a better photo in ''my opinion'' would have been the bride and groom slipping the rings on their hands... a close up of the hands slipping the rings on, because it denotes the ''action'' of deciding to commit forever. Because making a decision is an action, I think the photos should denote action.', '2005-06-03 10:56:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(1431127, 183695, 38401, '<td valign="top">I don''t feel that the image conveys instantly recognizable decision. Or rather, I don''t feel the need to make a decision. I understand that the boy could be making a decision... but for me it''s not rock solid. Kudos on the shot good color. I think an improvement would have been some friends heading down one path motioning the boy to follow, and then the boy looking down the other path as though ''deciding which one to go down''. For me this would have been a rock solid decision making photo... because the boy is put in the situation of having to make a decision. So 4 is my score for this photo.</td>', 'I don''t feel that the image conveys instantly recognizable decision. Or rather, I don''t feel the need to make a decision. I understand that the boy could be making a decision... but for me it''s not rock solid. Kudos on the shot good color. I think an improvement would have been some friends heading down one path motioning the boy to follow, and then the boy looking down the other path as though ''deciding which one to go down''. For me this would have been a rock solid decision making photo... because the boy is put in the situation of having to make a decision. So 4 is my score for this photo.', '2005-06-03 10:58:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(1431140, 183611, 38401, '<td valign="top">I didn''t feel that the image conveys instantly recognizable decision. But upon meditating about the subject, this is the universally ("THE USA") accepted method for proposing. Thus you have given the viewer the option of accepting. Seeing as how I''m a guy... this photo might have worked out better if there was another subject in the photo to accept. The other subject would not have been enough in that case though, they would have to be showing joy ("accepting") or pushing the ring away ("declining") to show that a decision by one party had been made. But since this photo would work for the other gender, I am giving it a 5.</td>', 'I didn''t feel that the image conveys instantly recognizable decision. But upon meditating about the subject, this is the universally ("THE USA") accepted method for proposing. Thus you have given the viewer the option of accepting. Seeing as how I''m a guy... this photo might have worked out better if there was another subject in the photo to accept. The other subject would not have been enough in that case though, they would have to be showing joy ("accepting") or pushing the ring away ("declining") to show that a decision by one party had been made. But since this photo would work for the other gender, I am giving it a 5.', '2005-06-03 11:04:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(1431152, 184008, 24951, '<td valign="top">Would have liked to see less foreground (ground) and not have the tips of the horns cut off - but I realize with a great animal action shot you have to take it or lose the entire event/action.9</td>', 'Would have liked to see less foreground (ground) and not have the tips of the horns cut off - but I realize with a great animal action shot you have to take it or lose the entire event/action.9', '2005-06-03 11:07:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(1431154, 183692, 38401, '<td valign="top">Good show. I think a way to improve this photo (and it might not have come out mind you) is to have exposed her long enough for her to remain solid in the middle and then have her walk down one of the paths as though she had decided to go down it (producing a ghost trail).</td>', 'Good show. I think a way to improve this photo (and it might not have come out mind you) is to have exposed her long enough for her to remain solid in the middle and then have her walk down one of the paths as though she had decided to go down it (producing a ghost trail).', '2005-06-03 11:07:32.000000', NULL, 1),
