(1437884, 182351, 35602, '<td valign="top">The lighting was very nice on this one.  I think the picture doesn''t work for this challenge.  I''d love to see this picture done with the upper front showing in the same light.  I saw one once done with this light, and the girl was looking out the window.  I actually sketched it I was so moved by the picture.</td>', 'The lighting was very nice on this one.  I think the picture doesn''t work for this challenge.  I''d love to see this picture done with the upper front showing in the same light.  I saw one once done with this light, and the girl was looking out the window.  I actually sketched it I was so moved by the picture.', '2005-06-06 22:31:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(1437887, 184003, 35602, '<td valign="top">The contrast was too strong around the person.</td>', 'The contrast was too strong around the person.', '2005-06-06 22:31:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(1437896, 184012, 31042, '<td valign="top">It''s a good thing this one got validated, otherwise, you might have risked entering such a beaut and missing out on the definite blue ribbon.  Keep up the awesome work, love it, speaks so many messages at once, more than a thousand words.  I love the tonal texture, and the useage of the rule of fifths in this one.  Fantastic manipulation of lighting in the post-processing, lost points on camera shake though, I can see the detail is slightly hazy.  Otherwise, and overall, fantastic well-put-together image!  Fabulous.  ......Now only if everyone else feels the same as me, we have a winner, and a site as corrupt as classic mutiny on the high seas.... Don''t judge me.  <br/> <br/>Simon<br/> <br/>www.simonphotography.net<br/> <br/>So who are you anyway, i don''t think there''s any risk in it...</td>', 'It''s a good thing this one got validated, otherwise, you might have risked entering such a beaut and missing out on the definite blue ribbon.  Keep up the awesome work, love it, speaks so many messages at once, more than a thousand words.  I love the tonal texture, and the useage of the rule of fifths in this one.  Fantastic manipulation of lighting in the post-processing, lost points on camera shake though, I can see the detail is slightly hazy.  Otherwise, and overall, fantastic well-put-together image!  Fabulous.  ......Now only if everyone else feels the same as me, we have a winner, and a site as corrupt as classic mutiny on the high seas.... Don''t judge me.   Simon www.simonphotography.net So who are you anyway, i don''t think there''s any risk in it...', '2005-06-06 22:38:37.000000', NULL, 1),
