(1445079, 183731, 37779, '<td valign="top">Thanks everyone for comments, positive or otherwise. I didn''t take this picture to appeal to anyone, to get points, or favorites, nor did I take the picture to offend or be insensitive. I took this picture because suicide is an evil, terrible, tragic thing. I took this picture for my grandfather..my Opa...who killed himself with a gun 3 years ago. He was a good man but unexpectedly made a terrible desicion which was hard hitting to me and my family. The results of such a selfish act are horrific, but the memories still exsist and you can never forget them. Because of his dry wit humor and kindness, his funeral was not sorrowful, but full of happiness and jokes. He would have wanted us to see it as him going out with a bang-- that was just the kind of man he was. <br/>As a teenager, I know countless instances of suicide attempts and the real deal from my peers. In my brother''s graduating class, there were 15 suicides in the school from that year. My step-sister had 3 friends kill themselves in her senior year, and I had a best friend end up in the hospital 2 times- that was in 8th grade. Even my sister had a classmate take her own life in 6th grade. It''s terrifying what an epidemic this is. It effects us all. Always remember to be nice to one another, that makes all the difference!  <br/></td>', 'Thanks everyone for comments, positive or otherwise. I didn''t take this picture to appeal to anyone, to get points, or favorites, nor did I take the picture to offend or be insensitive. I took this picture because suicide is an evil, terrible, tragic thing. I took this picture for my grandfather..my Opa...who killed himself with a gun 3 years ago. He was a good man but unexpectedly made a terrible desicion which was hard hitting to me and my family. The results of such a selfish act are horrific, but the memories still exsist and you can never forget them. Because of his dry wit humor and kindness, his funeral was not sorrowful, but full of happiness and jokes. He would have wanted us to see it as him going out with a bang-- that was just the kind of man he was. As a teenager, I know countless instances of suicide attempts and the real deal from my peers. In my brother''s graduating class, there were 15 suicides in the school from that year. My step-sister had 3 friends kill themselves in her senior year, and I had a best friend end up in the hospital 2 times- that was in 8th grade. Even my sister had a classmate take her own life in 6th grade. It''s terrifying what an epidemic this is. It effects us all. Always remember to be nice to one another, that makes all the difference!  ', '2005-06-10 00:45:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(1445411, 183475, 26849, '<td valign="top">Im amazed at all the comments about not seeing the decision in my entry.<br/> <br/>First of all no one sees a decision. The decision is not visible. Only the cause and effects. You may see the choices before during or after a decision. But the decision is in the mind. <br/> <br/>2nd  as a child you should have been told to make a wish before you blow on the dandelion plume. If you were never told you were cheated when you were young.<br/> <br/>Please check out this link. <a href="//www.flowgo.com/funpages/view.cfm/11793" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.flowgo.com/funpages/view.cfm/11793</a> <br/> <br/>The next time you pick up a dandelion plume make a wish before you blow. That brief moment when youre staring at the plume and making up your mind on what to wish for it what is captured in this photo. <br/> <br/>I did not realize how many never heard of this wishing opportunity. I knew the shot was not a great shot. It was entered because I thought it would be fun to remind a lot of you of your childhood memories. I never expected such a low score because they never knew about making a wish on a dandelion.<br/> <br/>For those that got it I hope you enjoyed it. And thanks for the two Favorite votes on the entry. <br/> <br/>Rod<br/><a href="//www.flowgo.com/funpages/view.cfm/11793" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Make your decision on what you will wish for.</a></td>', 'Im amazed at all the comments about not seeing the decision in my entry. First of all no one sees a decision. The decision is not visible. Only the cause and effects. You may see the choices before during or after a decision. But the decision is in the mind.  2nd  as a child you should have been told to make a wish before you blow on the dandelion plume. If you were never told you were cheated when you were young. Please check out this link. //www.flowgo.com/funpages/view.cfm/11793  The next time you pick up a dandelion plume make a wish before you blow. That brief moment when youre staring at the plume and making up your mind on what to wish for it what is captured in this photo.  I did not realize how many never heard of this wishing opportunity. I knew the shot was not a great shot. It was entered because I thought it would be fun to remind a lot of you of your childhood memories. I never expected such a low score because they never knew about making a wish on a dandelion. For those that got it I hope you enjoyed it. And thanks for the two Favorite votes on the entry.  RodMake your decision on what you will wish for.', '2005-06-10 05:37:56.000000', NULL, 0),
